hich issues one passes.pass1_chunk call per case per run'","calibrate_criterion loads spec = load_eval_spec(prompt_id) and iterates all_cases = spec.get('dataset'); no candidate/case-injection argument exists (src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:426-450)","Scope: 'Only criteria with no existing spec are written' — for such criteria load_eval_spec has no .rebar/evals file and falls back to _packaged_eval_spec or raises EvalError for an empty fire/no-fire set (eval.py:76-78, 433-437)"],"finding":"The admission run routes each unadmitted mined candidate through calibrate_criterion, but that function evaluates a criterion's already-persisted fixture dataset (loaded via load_eval_spec(prompt_id)) — it exposes no parameter to inject a single not-yet-written candidate case; and since the plan's scope is criteria with NO existing spec, load_eval_spec will fall back to a packaged spec or raise EvalError on an absent/empty fire-nofire dataset, so the named path cannot run the candidate as-is.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9fa04981bdd31ddf","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Admission run'; eval.py → calibrate_criterion / load_eval_spec","norm_id":"n9f3c2ad05e78a445","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Admitting a candidate for a criterion that ships no packaged fixture: calibrate_criterion raises EvalError before any run","A candidate case whose material is not in the persisted dataset never gets its own three runs"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Feed the candidate case(s) directly to the finder path (the solve(prompt_id, case) call and its majority-of-3 obs_fire computation) rather than through calibrate_criterion's whole-fixture loader, or introduce an explicit candidate-cases argument to calibrate_criterion; then map obs_fire (already a strict majority of 3) to REPRODUCES.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"high","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the admitted candidate's blocking/advisory posture is recorded and consumed — the exact key (and whether it lives in the eval spec or in criteria routing) and which reader acts on it.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'written to `.rebar/evals/<prompt-id>.eval.yaml`, carrying `blocking` posture when the selector tiered it as blocking and `advisory` otherwise'","src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py:275-320 — validate_eval_spec recognizes prompt/model/epochs/gate/coverage_threshold/scorers/dataset/gold_set; no posture field","src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-T10.eval.yaml — a packaged spec carries no posture key","default_posture is a routing key: src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json and registry.py:40 ('default_posture': 'advisory'|'blocking')"],"finding":"The plan writes a `blocking`/`advisory` posture onto each admitted eval spec, but posture is a routing concept (`default_posture` in criteria_routing.json), not a field in the eval-spec schema; the plan never defines the field name it will use on the spec, its allowed values, or which consumer reads it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1f09c8d77a37a1e7","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Disposition","norm_id":"n0c1346b10af5d952","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An admitted spec is written with posture metadata that no eval-spec reader consumes, or with a key name that diverges from what the plan-review gate's blocking-decision path expects."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add an acceptance criterion that exercises a fatal error mid-criterion and asserts (a) no partial spec is written for the incomplete criterion and (b) a re-run resumes at the first uncompleted criterion.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E1","E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'A criterion is atomic: its spec is written only after all of its candidates finish their three runs, so a partial criterion never lands.'","'a later re-run resumes at the first uncompleted criterion'","No AC asserts that a mid-criterion fatal error leaves no partial spec, nor that a re-run resumes correctly."],"finding":"The Failure-disposition guarantees — a criterion is atomic (its spec written only after all its candidates finish), a fatal BudgetExceeded stops the run with previously-completed criteria admitted, and a later re-run resumes at the first uncompleted criterion — are described deliverables with no covering acceptance criterion. AC2 verifies BudgetExceeded raises with zero calls, but no AC verifies partial-criterion atomicity or the resume-on-rerun behavior.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fde98eb9670fb0041","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Failure disposition; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"ndec606bd0f8c2d3a","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A fatal error mid-criterion leaves a half-written spec that a re-run then double-processes or skips."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a pytest-driven AC: script a fatal BudgetExceeded during a criterion's runs, assert the incomplete criterion produced no .eval.yaml file while earlier criteria did, then re-invoke and assert it begins at the uncompleted criterion.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unv